<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhai Zhao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 393</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhai Zhao was the second and last ruler of Zhai Wei, a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingling">Dingling</a> state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-kingdoms">Sixteen Kingdoms</a> period. He succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhai-liao">Zhai Liao</a> in 391, but in 392 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-chui">Murong Chui</a> of the Later Yan forced the river crossing and took his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hua-county">Huatai</a>. Zhai Zhao fled to the Western Yan, where he was later executed for plotting.</p></div>
